 ],
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "text": "What if Africa united and tried taking over the world?",
   "s": 0.0,
   "e": 3.36
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "text": "54 countries. One flag. Overnight, the United States of Africa is born.",
   "s": 4.46,
   "e": 9.78
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "text": "It's bigger than the US, China and India combined, with 1.5 billion people.",
   "s": 10.32,
   "e": 15.96
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "text": "Its army? Roughly 2 million soldiers.",
   "s": 16.44,
   "e": 18.98
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "text": "And it controls the world's supply chain. About 70% of the cobalt in your phone battery is mined in Africa.",
   "s": 19.48,
   "e": 26.0
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "text": "First move: close the Suez Canal. Now ships between Europe and Asia have to sail all the way around... Africa.",
   "s": 26.52,
   "e": 33.95
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "text": "Then it crosses the 14 kilometer Strait of Gibraltar into Spain, and jumps from Tunisia to Sicily.",
   "s": 34.48,
   "e": 40.58
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "text": "Across the Red Sea, Arabia is only 26 kilometers away.",
